finding: The example does not deliver the host-controlled first-frame handoff it claims: `examples/loading-screen/src/main.ts:19-23,54-60` makes `complete()` wait for a button, then reports “host revealed first frame” while `remove()` only removes Shallot's overlay and the same poster remains; there is no first frame or reveal action. `examples/loading-screen/shallot.json:3-4` declares that as the recipe's user promise, and README:9 repeats it. It also has no retained example check: `src/standard/loading/index.test.ts:71-116` only checks mocked DOM/styles, while the browser assertions were a one-off script with no retained result. Screenshots do not prove the interactive handoff or protect it against regression. Thus the implementation and declared evidence fail the example/check claim. Separately, the accepted Check's browser criterion (“host content through loading and handoff”) is too weak to require a first-frame handoff: the unchanged poster satisfies it. Clarify that criterion to observe the host-controlled transition/reveal, and retain the browser check; the unit CSS assertions do not themselves expose this gap.
